# Validate a dotfiles branch on a clean macOS image.
#
# Nothing is mounted from the host on purpose: the whole point is that the
# guest clones from GitHub the way a fresh machine would, so a step that only
# works because of state already on this laptop fails here instead of on the
# next new machine.

tart clone ghcr.io/cirruslabs/macos-golden-gate-base:latest gg-validate
tart set gg-validate --cpu 6 --memory 12288 --disk-size 90
tart run --no-graphics gg-validate &
ssh admin@$(tart ip gg-validate)     # admin / admin

# inside the guest, either path:
#   Nix path      -> README, "macOS setup (Darwin)"
#   no-Nix path   -> curl -fsSL .../tools/mise/bootstrap.sh | sh
#                    then: mise run gh-login

tart stop gg-validate && tart delete gg-validate

# Host-version caveat. This machine is macOS 15 and tart is pinned to 2.34.0
# (lib/tart.nix: 2.35+ hard-links libSwiftCompatibilitySpan, which only exists
# on macOS 26). A guest newer than the host is not guaranteed to boot. Tahoe
# (macOS 26) did on 2026-07-01 (#35); Golden Gate is untested here. If it
# refuses to boot, swap golden-gate -> tahoe and every other step is identical.

# Runnable: just -g tart-new gg-validate
